  "body": "Part of #2007. Stacked on #2002 (tool settings go into Properties).\n\nMaintainer in chat, 2026-11-15: \"That tool editor issue is a P3\".\n\n## What happens\n\n`tool_editor_window` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs:594-893`) is a modal window with 3 columns. Column 1 (L625-846) puts each label above its input: `field(ui, \"Diameter\")`, then `num(...)`.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Show the tool settings in the Properties tool page as a property grid. Put the labels to the left of the inputs. Use the helpers in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/layout/form.rs` and `fields.rs` (#1122).\n- Use collapsible groups: Geometry, Holder, Cutting data, Catalog.\n- Retire the modal window when #2002 moves the catalog to its own dock panel. This also removes the cause of #2003.\n- Keep each file below about 400 lines (`crates/ui/AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Done means:\n\n- Each tool field shows its label to the left of its input, in a collapsible group.\n- The structural test (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs`) pins the labels, the groups and the label-left order.\n- Each edit is still one undoable `ChangeTool` command.\n- No snapshot PNG changes.\n- The PR has before and after screenshots.\n\nOrder: first of the sub-issues. It needs #2002.\n",
